Chunk note: 45 RS-zoned properties within 100m of a Valley Line SE stop, in a panel restricted to mature RS zoning (so this is a narrower, RS-only version of the positive control, not all VLSE-adjacent properties citywide). If this shows a discrete post-2023 jump, it demonstrates the assessment mechanically responds to *some* coded proximity influence within this data and FE structure -- validating that a null on the ZBR test is a real null, not a design limitation. If it shows nothing, that is also reportable: it would mean this design cannot detect *any* neighbour-influence toggle at this timescale, which bounds how much weight the ZBR null itself can bear.



